    "details": {
      "description": "<p>An ancient Dwarven invention, this rune inscribed mine cart moves on its own, and has been enchanted to provide protection from the Stonewyrm’s Breath effect.</p><p>Stonewyrm's Breath is listed here for ease of reference.</p><hr /><p><strong>Stonewyrm’s Breath</strong></p><p><em>[Environmental][Primal][Magical][Poison]</em></p><p>Poisonous gas wells up from the bottom of the catacombs. Creatures that end their turn within the area of the hazard must attempt a <strong>#DC#</strong> (@Check[type:fortitude|dc:XX]) Fortitude Save or become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 1}. If the creature was already Slowed, its Slowed value instead increases by 1 on a failed save. If a creature becomes unable to act due to the slowed condition from this effect, it becomes permanently @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.dTwPJuKgBQCMxixg]{Petrified}. A creature’s Slowed condition reduces by 1 each time it ends its turn outside the hazard’s area.</p><p>Stonewyrm’s Breath is a magical effect that cannot be counteracted. Spells or other abilities that would cleanse the air (such as Cleanse Air) have their durations reduced to 1 round. Effects that provide breathable air (such as an Everair Mask) do not protect from Stonewyrm’s Breath - this deep in the catacombs, it is not an inhaled effect.</p>",
